WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.311
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.450
SPEAKER: BigQuery can process
enormous amounts of data.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.210
Adding cost controls can protect
you from runaway queries,

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.880
whether you have multiple
BigQuery projects and users,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.410
or it's just you.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.930
You can manage costs by
setting a custom quota that

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.630
specifies a limit on the
amount of query data processed

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:22.700
per day.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.200
This video will take you through
the process of establishing

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.090
your own custom quotas.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.060
You may set quotas to control
costs at the project level

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.770
or at the user level.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.710
Project level custom quotas
limit the aggregate usage

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.550
of all users in that project,
while user level custom quotas

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.160
are separately applied
to each user or service

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.050
account within a project.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.030
You may use either of
these quota options,

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.980
or both in tandem.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.010
Used in tandem, usage will
count against both quotas

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.680
and adhere to the stricter
of the two limits.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.530
An example scenario can be found
at the documentation linked

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.640
below.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.770
Start by navigating
to the Quotas menu

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:02.270
in the IAM and Admin console.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:06.640
Make sure you have the
right project selected.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.355
Filter the quotas for
the BigQuery API service.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:17.090
Check the box for Query Usage
Per Day and/or Query Usage

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.065
Per Day Per User.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.920
And click Edit Quotas.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.200
Set your email and phone number.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.780
These contact details may
be used when processing

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.920
certain quota requests.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.830
Enter your daily
quotas in tebibytes.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.850
Notice that the quotas
are in tebibytes,

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.630
so be sure to make any
necessary conversions.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:44.470
Click Done and then
click Submit Request.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.560
Review the changes
and click Confirm.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.840
Quota changes should take
effect within a few minutes.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.800
Once the quotas are set, if
project level or user level

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.700
custom quotas are exceeded,
BigQuery returns an error.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.940
Daily quotas reset at
midnight Pacific Time.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.220
For more information
on custom quotas please

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.400
visit the documentation
and FAQs linked below.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.600
Happy analyzing.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.950
[MUSIC PLAYING]

